{"title":"Career roadmap · Policy Analyst","role":"Policy Analyst","summary":"A Policy Analyst researches public problems, evaluates policies and programmes, analyses evidence, and develops recommendations for governments, think tanks, NGOs and international organisations. A BA in Public Administration provides a strong foundation in governance, public policy, administrative systems, economics, law and research methods.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Public Administration"},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Strong direct alignment. Entry-level roles are more commonly titled Policy Research Assistant, Research Associate, Programme Analyst or Policy Associate before progressing to Policy Analyst."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a competitive modern policy career, add statistics, data analysis, policy evaluation, economics, GIS, public finance and strong policy writing."}]},{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Public Administration","Policy Research Internship","Research/Policy Assistant","Policy Associate/Research Associate","Policy Analyst","Senior Policy Analyst","Policy Lead/Programme Director","Policy Research Director"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build public-policy, governance, economics, statistics, research and writing skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in a policy domain such as health, education, climate, technology, finance or urban development."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Lead policy research, programme evaluation and stakeholder-facing projects."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward policy leadership, think-tank direction, government advisory or international-development roles."}]]}]},{"heading":